  "lines": 178,
  "scope": "Actual repeated calls to the literal flag-filter return the ordered list of the same child outputs. The explicit atom bound is twice the input flag-cell count plus five times the draw count plus two. A normalized finite product law equals the original product measure and the output-law transport is exact for all repetitions, including zero draws. Original flag rows and canonical typed input enumeration remain supplied; random source generation, efficient seed/forest construction and physical bit runtime remain separate."
